Suppose you run:

ping google.com

And get:

Temporary failure in name resolution

This means:

Ubuntu could not find the IP address for google.com.

It does not automatically mean the internet is completely down.

Maybe:

DNS server is not reachable
DNS configuration is wrong
Network is not working
DNS service has a problem
Troubleshooting approach

First test the IP:

ping -c 3 8.8.8.8

Then test the name:

ping -c 3 google.com
Understand
Ping IP works
Ping name fails
        ↓
Possible DNS problem
